<p>The town hosts its own holiday, Hopkins Day, and welcomes people for the=
ir celebration on Garifuna Independence Day as well. They do this with drum=
 ceremonies that can last until the early hours of the morning.</p>
<p>The village is separated into two parts; the Northside (Baila) and the S=
outhside (False Sittee). Hopkins is surrounded by the Maya Mountains and th=
e Cockscomb Range inland, and the Caribbean Sea on its shore. It is also ve=
ry close to the Sittee River.</p></div>
